{"changes":["exchange/builder.go: toUnit projects sourcePromptHash, confidence with hasConfidence, sourceCommitSha and captureMeta; exchange/artifact.go reverses it","exchange/integrate.go: one artifactCaptureMeta type feeds both renderers; artifactConfidence and artifactCaptureMetaFor emit nil unless a value was declared, so an artifact that declared nothing re-exports byte-identically","conformance/artifact.go: the envelope checks moved out of analyzeJSON into classifyEnvelope, called by both adapters; captureMetaKeys is one list feeding both the shape diagnostic and the unknown-field refusal","exchange/model.go: hasConfidence carries a declared zero, which omitempty would otherwise drop from unit.json; a non-zero value counts as declared for packages written before the flag"],"role":"implementation","summary":"The rest of the ADR-035 envelope did not survive transport. sourcePromptHash, confidence, sourceCommitSha and captureMeta were never projected into the exchange unit, and validUntil, lastConfirmed and the capture fields were never rendered back, so export dropped them with no finding. The Markdown adapter read none of them either, which made any render-only fix write-only for Markdown-native repositories.","tests":["exchange/envelope_test.go: full envelope round-trips byte-identically through both adapters, the explicit 0.0 stays a declared zero, an envelope-free artifact gains nothing, and sha256(captureMeta.title) equals dedupeKey on both fixtures","conformance/envelope_test.go TestAnalyzeMarkdownReadsEnvelope, TestAnalyzeJSONAndMarkdownAgreeOnEnvelope, TestAnalyzeEnvelopeRefusals: both adapters read the same five fields and refuse the same eleven malformed values"]}